BND-11: restore the hot-started groundwater flow as both old and new flow

gwater_getState() saves gw->newFlow, but gwater_setState() restored it into
gw->oldFlow only and left newFlow at the 0 set by gwater_initState(). The
first runoff step of the continuation shifts newFlow into oldFlow, so the
restored value was discarded: routing interpolated the groundwater inflow
from 0, and about half of the first runoff step's groundwater volume never
reached the node, although the aquifer state drained by the full amount.
Restore the saved flow into newFlow as well, so that the first step starts
from it, as in the uninterrupted run.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-11_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
index d511143..945ee77 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
@@ -457,6 +457,7 @@ void gwater_setState(int subcatchIndex, double x[])
     gw->theta = x[0];
     gw->lowerDepth = x[1] - gw->bottomElev;
     gw->oldFlow = x[2];
+    gw->newFlow = x[2];
     if ( x[3] != MISSING ) gw->maxInfilVol = x[3];
 }
 
